ents.Topics: ADF Web Components (af:table, af:form), Partial Page Rendering (PPR) listeners, visual skins.🛠️ Practical Exercise:Build an administrative portal layout (hr-dashboard.jsf).Establish an asynchronous parent-child layout using component triggers: selecting a corporate division in the master pane immediately filters target staff records in the secondary data table without a full-page browser refresh.Day 4: Transition to Microservices – ADF REST Web ServicesObjective: Expose legacy monolithic ADF objects as standardized REST endpoints.Topics: REST Framework Configurations, JSON payload manipulation, mapping view attributes to resource properties.🛠️ Practical Exercise:In JDeveloper 14c, create an administrative REST Web Service project.Expose EmployeesVO as a JSON schema resource endpoint.Configure custom GET filters (e.g., query staff matching salary > 5000).Verify the exposed endpoints locally using Postman (http://localhost:7101/hr-app/rest/v1/employees).Day 5: Introduction to Project Spectra & BOSS ArchitectureObjective: Learn the architecture of Oracle Cloud Native Services (Project Spectra) and BOSS (Business Object Spectra Service).Topics: Helidon microservice core, stateless microservices, consumption of BOSS OpenAPI schemas.🛠️ Practical Exercise:Generate a stateless Helidon SE microservice template via Terminal:bashhelidon init
